Fix a crash at every map load with -nosound: S_ClearOverflow() dereferences
known_sfx, which S_Init() only allocates when sound starts.

  Program received signal SIGSEGV, Segmentation fault.
  S_ClearOverflow: ldw ret0(r5),r3  (Host_ClearMemory, "Clearing memory")

Signed-off-by: René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

--- a/common/snd_dma.c
+++ b/common/snd_dma.c
@@ -280,6 +280,8 @@ void
 S_ClearOverflow()
 {
     S_StopAllSounds(true);
+    if (!known_sfx)
+	return;
     struct known_sfx *known = known_sfx->overflow;
 
     while (known) {
